   "text": "Ba2NaO (mp-1019519) alone accounts for the main peaks; this rests on a rough, hand-calculated peak comparison.\n\n1. **Excluding the perovskites.** Ca2MnWO6, Eu2MnRhO6, Sr3CaTi4O12 and LaCuO3 all have pseudocubic cells near 3.9\u20133.97 \u00c5. Their strongest lines fall at about 31\u201332.7\u00b0. None of them explains the dominant split peak at 33.6/34.2\u00b0 or the 25.6\u00b0 doublet.\n2. **Excluding the rock-salt types.** Li4Fe3WO8 and Li3Mg(NiO2)4 should give strong lines near 37\u00b0, 43\u00b0 and 63\u00b0. These are not observed with any strength.\n3. **Excluding the other two.** ZnTiO3 (ilmenite) and ZnCu(WO4)2 (wolframite type) fit the observed peak set poorly.\n4. **Matching Ba2NaO.** Its cell converts to a C-centred orthorhombic cell of about 6.66 \u00d7 15.57 \u00d7 6.98 \u00c5. The calculated positions match most observed peaks:\n\n| Calculated (hkl) | Calculated 2\u03b8 | Observed 2\u03b8 |\n|---|---|---|\n| (111) | 19.3\u00b0 | weak ~19.0\u201319.4\u00b0 |\n| (040) | 22.8\u00b0 | 22.6\u00b0 |\n| (131) | 25.2\u00b0 | 25.4\u00b0 (doublet) |\n| (002) | 25.5\u00b0 | 25.7\u00b0 (doublet) |\n| (221) | 31.9\u00b0 | 32.0\u00b0 |\n| (132) | 33.7\u00b0 | 33.6\u00b0 |\n| (151) | 34.3\u00b0 | 34.2\u00b0 |\n| (060) | 34.5\u00b0 | 34.2\u00b0 |\n| (240) | 35.4\u00b0 | 35.0\u00b0 |\n| (023) | 40.4\u00b0 | 40.6\u00b0 |\n| (310) | 41.0\u00b0 | 40.6\u201342.0\u00b0 |\n| (113) | 41.5\u00b0 | 42.0\u00b0 |\n\n5. **Caveats.** Calculated low-angle lines at 11.4\u00b0 and 14.5\u00b0 are not seen, and (220) near 29\u00b0 is absent. These were not checked against structure factors. I did not test whether a second phase contributes to the 32.0\u00b0 peak.\n\n{\"present\": [\"mp-1019519\"], \"confidence\": 0.6, \"note\": \"Ba2NaO's C-centred orthorhombic cell reproduces the main peaks at 22.6, 25.5, 32.0, 33.6/34.2, 35 and 40.6-42 degrees, while the perovskite, rock-salt and other candidates do not fit the dominant 33.6/34.2 doublet.\"}",
